    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i need a step by step guide on how we should roll out MFA across our law firm using hardware security keys like yubikeys instead of the usual sms stuff. we want to move away from sms because of the interception risks. need a plan for deployment and how to onboard the staff without making it a huge mess.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "1. Evaluate Current MFA Setup: Review your existing MFA systems in detail to understand the existing setup, identify users who will be affected by the transition, and uncover potential areas of resistance.\n\n2. Define MPA Policy: Develop an MPA User Policy to outline the reasons and benefits of moving to hardware security keys, along with the required steps to ensure a smooth transition.\n\n3. Plan Deployment: Decide whether you will make this change across the entire firm initially or in phases. Once you've done that, schedule a date and create a communication about when and why the change will happen.\n\n4. Choose Hardware: Purchase the necessary hardware security keys, like YubiKeys and make sure they are compatible with important applications (such as CRM, email, cloud services, etc.) your firm uses.\n\n5. Evaluate Software: Evaluate MFA software that supports hardware keys and ensure it's compatible with the software and applications used by the law firm.\n\n6. Test Coach: Consider hiring or training a few key employees and make them MVPs (Most Valuable Pupils) who can then train others. They could easily become frustrated if they're slow to get accustomed to the change.\n\n7. Train Staff: Inform your employees through a combination of in-person training, webinars, email, and",
      "source": "target",
